# Asima OS runtime mounts (after switch-root).
# /, /usr, /etc, /var, /home, /root, /var/lib/{containers,libvirt,flatpak}, /run/asimaos-snapshots
# and /run/initramfs/reserve are mounted in the initramfs by asimaos-early-mount.service, from the
# encrypted or plain pool alike.
# <device>               <mountpoint>            <type>  <options>                                                    <dump> <pass>
# The ESP (start menu, boot images, Asima Rescue) never opens by itself: an accident,
# a careless script or malware running as administrator can't reach it. The services that need it
# (updates, "mark as good", Asima Maintenance) open it in their own private mount namespace.
# An administrator can still open it by hand: mount /boot
PARTLABEL=ESP            /boot                   vfat    umask=0077,noauto                                            0 0
